Martin Read wrote on 31 Mar 2011 19:19:54 +0100 (BST):
> Undead Hippo <hostilnakfor@yahoo.com> wrote:
> >I understand there is general disdain for NethackW with the nice icons
> >here.  Can you explain why you feel your disdain is justified?
> 
> Because a purple '&' is a hell of a lot scarier than a 16x16 blob that
> might just possibly be some kind of demon.

Exactly.  I dislike tiles because all the ones I've seen are *worse* than 
simple colored ascii. 


Furthermore, over the years I've grown to like the simplicity of the 
letters -- my brain can more quickly interpret them.  To me, an "L" is 
not a malevolent undead sorcerer like those in various DND-related 
fantasy fiction, but a collection of attacks, defenses, and other 
properties which can affect the game.  It isn't anything like this:
http://www.celestialheavens.com/heroespedia/images/0/0c/HOMM5
_Necropolis_Creature_Lich.jpg


